# lesson1 – BankAccount and Object Properties in C#

This project demonstrates encapsulation and property usage in C# through a simple `BankAccount` class.

## Concepts Covered

- Auto-properties (`OwnerName`)
- Read-only properties (`Balance`)
- Backing fields (`_balance`)
- Input validation in methods (`Deposit`, `Withdraw`)
- Constructor-based initialization

## Code Overview

```csharp
var account = new BankAccount("Alice", 1000m);
account.Deposit(250m);
account.Withdraw(100m);
Console.WriteLine(account.Balance); // 1150


